[29.541158, "o", "454: \r\n  1455: ## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n  1456: \r\n  1457: Mid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n  1458: amendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n  1459: only, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's\r\n  1460: ledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n  1461: in effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n  1462: before any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n  1463: mail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n  1464: \r\n  1465: ## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment — supporting chronology\r\n  1466: \r\n  1467: Tax counsel flagged lease modification restatement restatement risk during August memo close, unrelated to extractor precedence but relevant to why the archive retains full correspondence.\r\n  1468: \r\n  1469: Platform engin"]
