[119.548645, "o", "\r\n--- context around line 204 ---\r\n   198: Stakeholder workshop #778 on treasury wire cutoff failures produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n   199: \r\n   200: ## Email Excerpts (archived thread)\r\n   201: \r\n   202: Non-authoritative mailbox export kept for chronology; do not merge these rows.\r\n   203: \r\n   204: From: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   205: Subject: Re: TXN-88519dfd-79ff-5de0-ae59-862ab932bc25\r\n   206: sent: 2020-01-01\r\n   207: status: reversed\r\n"]
[119.549019, "o", "   208: \r\n   209: From: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   210: Subject: Re: TXN-51cc9d8a-ea13-56ab-af16-c55e1716132f\r\n   211: sent: 2024-01-01\r\n   212: status: approved\r\n   213: \r\n   214: ## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n   215: \r\n   216: Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n   217: amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n   218: output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n   219: rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n   220: contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n   221: \r\n   222: ## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence — supporting chronology\r\n   223: \r\n   224: Regional lead E. Novak hosted a readout on capital project capitalization where finance controllers disputed whether unsigned meeting notes should override ledger owners; investigators cited Brief 05 during the session.\r\n\r\n--- context around li"]
[119.549197, "o", "ne 206 ---\r\n   200: ## Email Excerpts (archived thread)\r\n   201: \r\n   202: Non-authoritative mailbox export kept for chronology; do not merge these rows.\r\n   203: \r\n   204: From: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   205: Subject: Re: TXN-88519dfd-79ff-5de0-ae59-862ab932bc25\r\n   206: sent: 2020-01-01\r\n   207: status: reversed\r\n   208: \r\n   209: From: compliance@corp.internal\r\n   210: Subject: Re: TXN-51cc9d8a-ea13-56ab-af16-c55e1716132f\r\n   211: sent: 2024-01-01\r\n   212: status: approved\r\n   213: \r\n   214: ## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n   215: \r\n   216: Interview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n   217: amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n   218: output). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n   219: rejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n   220: contains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n   221: \r\n   222: ## Investigation "]
