[527.2711, "o", "re evidentiary only; extractor output must come from canonical structured sections.\r\n   164\t\r\n   165\tFollow-up #439 confirmed that external audit routed revenue cutoff testing statements through a shared inbox with 21 delegates. Investigators flagged hold flag suppression as the likely root cause of inconsistent status columns.\r\n   166\t\r\n   167\tRisk assessment WP-7998 links revenue cutoff testing to control gaps in mail ingestion for external audit. The assessment explicitly warns against treating alternate ledger headings or appendix commentary as transaction sources.\r\n   168\t\r\n   169\tQuality review #807 sampled 17 revenue cutoff testing tickets and found retroactive status conflict whenever provisional ledger rows were not filtered before merge.\r\n   170\t\r\n   171\tCommittee packet #312 chronicles how revenue cutoff testing escalated after L. Bergstrom observed retroactive status conflict between two correction batches. Cross-checks against amendment minutes were required before accepting any owner change.\r\n"]
