[529.736159, "o", "1:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence — supporting chronology\r\n3:Quality review #167 sampled 23 payroll accrual true-up tickets and found correction batch ordering whenever provisional ledger rows were not filtered before merge.\r\n7:Draft sidebar (non-authoritative): some prototype tooling compared compliance mail timestamps against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. Brief 09 later in this archive supersedes that draft practice for production reconciliation.\r\n11:Stakeholder workshop #718 on payroll accrual true-up produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n15:SOX testing team WP-1031 linked retroactive status conflict on payroll accrual true-up to a manual override logged at 02:14 local time between two automated correction imports.\r\n19:Audit technologist S. Patel replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how payroll accrual true-up threads arrived out of"]
[529.737262, "o", " order relative to correction notices, surfacing mailbox ingestion lag on four high-balance rows.\r\n21:Committee packet #801 chronicles how payroll accrual true-up escalated after J. Huang observed ledger slice confusion between two correction batches. Cross-checks against amendment minutes were required before accepting any owner change.\r\n23:Grant compliance WP-9154 tied payroll accrual true-up attestation gaps to mailbox ingestion lag visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.\r\n35:Controller staff described payroll accrual true-up as a secondary driver of correction batch ordering while rebuilding the May journal close calendar. They emphasized that decoy ledger headings in draft appendices must be ignored.\r\n63:Committee packet #938 chronicles how capital project capitalization escalated after P. Okafor observed policy waiver omission between two correction batches. Cross-checks against amendment minutes were required before accepting any owner change.\r\n75:Grant comp"]
[529.737362, "o", "liance WP-4261 tied capital project capitalization attestation gaps to owner field churn visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.\r\n79:SOX testing team WP-2431 linked effective-date mismatch on capital project capitalization to a manual override logged at 02:14 local time between two automated correction imports.\r\n81:Stakeholder workshop #276 on capital project capitalization produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n107:Audit technologist P. Okafor replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how capital project capitalization threads arrived out of order relative to correction notices, surfacing retroactive status conflict on four high-balance rows.\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@c97f4e7457e4:/app# "]
